 "hunting": {
  "about": "HUNTING (#156, doc/land-civilisation.md): animals wander the wilderness near players — the world server keeps them (scripts/land_server.py herd): up to per_area within area metres of each player, spawned 18-40 m away on dry land by the biome's kinds, wandering, and fleeing at full speed from a player within flee metres; gone when no player is within keep metres. A weapon strikes one within its reach (a spear close, a bow far, spending an arrow); a strike costs strike_s of work; at 0 hp it drops its items into the hunter's bag. Animals only — weapons never touch a player. AGGRESSION (#162, operator: \"add aggressive deer and death/respawn mechanism\"): a share of each kind (angry) charge a player within charge metres and strike within strike_reach every strike_s for its damage; any animal struck by a hunter fights back the same way if its kind has damage. BALLISTICS AND THE KNIFE (#157, operator: \"ballistics? bow and arrow? knife? carpentry tools?\"): a bow shoots an arrow along the player's look at `draw` m/s; it falls under g, takes its time to arrive and hits an animal only where the animal is when the arrow gets there — a running one must be led, a far one aimed above; an arrow that misses lands, and some (`recover`) can be picked up where they fell for drop_s seconds. A kill gives its meat to anyone; its `butcher` items (hide, bone) only to a hunter with a knife.",
