 "market": {
  "about": "MARKETS (#161, doc/land-civilisation.md; operator 2026-11-09: \"local markets first, global only with the invention of the internet\", \"trading stands\"). An offer is made standing at a trading stand (within at metres of one) and lives there; it is seen and taken only by a player standing at a stand within reach metres of it — the stands of one market. A gift is handed over in person (within hand metres). On every offer taken the maker receives what it asked for less fee of each item (rounded down) — a sink that grows with trade itself. PRICES (#163: \"we need currencies of all types so we need a flexible value system based on supply and demand\"): every offer taken is a trade on the record; the going rate of X in Y at a market is the volume-weighted ratio of the market's trades of X for Y within window_s, each weighing half as much every half_life_s; X and Y that never traded directly are priced through the items that link them, the best-traded path first. No item has a fixed price — coins included: a coin is worth what the market gives for it.",
  "at": 6,
  "reach": 64,
  "hand": 8,
  "fee": 0.05,
  "window_s": 604800,
  "half_life_s": 172800,
  "keep_trades": 20000
 },
 "health": {
